Z||000000||Haze_Performance||02-14-2001||06:07 AM||||Ok..I got the '87 SE running. The Alternator is in and doing well  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ..Now when I start the car it will stumble and slighty backfire. And if I let it run for 15 to 20 mins. it will die out. Even if I give it gas it still dies. Im not getting any codes. I have a new O2, Cap, Rotor, Wires, Plugs, Alternator & TPS.<P>I had alot of trouble finding the correct position for the Distributor (I had to pull it out to replace the O-Ring) but I think its right. Just to test it I tried 1 tooth back & 1 forward. Its now in the only place that the car will start in. My timing mark is still all over the place. (I timed it right. I grounded the computer first) Im kinda lost on this now. I was thinking about replacing the Distributor (It had some rust on it + the 2 wires that goto the module dont have the connecter on them anymore. The the two wires are just pluged into the module) & Module (Just for the hell of it). What else can I do. I also checked all the vac. lines for leaks. (There all good) <P>Just to let it be known... Theres an ADS Super Chip in it. Im not sure if that affects the timing? I also know the car needs a new catalytic converter. (Its rattling like a B*T*H when I start it)<P>I would be greatfull for advice you can give & Thank You to those who have been helped me before.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P><BR>TFTS  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Carl (The guy that needs to get this damn car running before his wife  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> kills  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> him  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> )<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif"> </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||11
Z||000001||Motorhead||02-14-2001||06:48 AM||||Carl,<BR>Did you double check that plug wires are connected in proper firing order?  I know this sounds obvious, but in my zeal to put an engine back together I've gotten the order wrong before with similar results. Boy was my face red.   <BR>Mike<P>------------------<BR>"The one who dies with the most toys wins!"<BR>  bluewater46@hotmail.com<BR>1986 coupe<BR>1984 coupe<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1372350&a=10234998&p=38686771&Sequence=0">  <p>[This message has been edited by Motorhead (edited 02-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||02-14-2001||06:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Motorhead:<BR><B>Carl,<BR>Did you double check that plug wires are connected in proper firing order?  I know this sounds obvious, but in my zeal to put an engine back together I've gotten the order wrong before with similar results. Boy was my face red.   <BR>Mike<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes Sir... All the plug wires are correct.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif"> </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||10
