Z||000005||Haze_Performance||02-14-2001||02:45 PM||||Also let me add... When I first start it up theres a <B>large amount of VERY FOUL smelling</B> white-ish grey smoke coming out of the exhaust. (For about a min. or two) Theres no cracked head... No oil in the coolant or water in the oil.<P>I am so lost...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif"> </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||10
Z||000006||SloPonti||02-15-2001||12:19 AM||||the smoke on startup is oil burning! the valve seals are old and brittle and will leak oil past the seals and down on top of the cylinder head and so when you first start it up it burns the oil off! this does not really hurt anything except burns oil! just shows signs of an older motor! my 87 iroc used to do this but i replaced the valve seals and now no smoke! this problem should not have anything to do with the cars performance!! hope this helps!<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000007||Haze_Performance||02-15-2001||10:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SloPonti:<BR><B>the smoke on startup is oil burning! the valve seals are old and brittle and will leak oil past the seals and down on top of the cylinder head and so when you first start it up it burns the oil off! this does not really hurt anything except burns oil! just shows signs of an older motor! my 87 iroc used to do this but i replaced the valve seals and now no smoke! this problem should not have anything to do with the cars performance!! hope this helps!<BR>Rob</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Rob,<BR>  Its a little more severe than oil burn start up. When I picked up the car there was none. Now without driving it at all, it has started smoking. (Only after replacing the Dis.) I think I killed the timing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <P>The damn thing just wont run.... Im going to replace the Distributor, Module & Catalytic. If this doent work I think Im gonna part it out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Thanks for the Advice Guys.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   <BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif"> </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>PFF Members Photo Page</A><BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1431213" TARGET=_blank><BR>Photopoint Gallery</A>||||reg||9
Z||000008||1FST2M6||02-15-2001||10:48 AM||||you said you replaced the TPS.. did you check it's voltage? if you don'tre-install it in the correct position your voltage will be off and cause symptoms similar to what you are describing. it the cats ratteling thats means it's not clogged just crappy and the car will run with a displaced monolith. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Formula88||02-15-2001||03:32 PM||||Are the insides of the exhaust pipes oily and sooty?  If they're not, the cloud could be debris from the converter blowing out.  If it is sooty (even damp to the touch) you're burning and blowing out oil.  Unhook the exhaust first.  Do all the cylinders have good compression?  If the compression drops as you're cranking, that's a sign of exhaust blockage.||||reg||3
Z||000010||ToddAsh||02-17-2001||04:29 PM|||| Changed my Daughters Cat Conv last week. Stumbled,no pwer on highway.Chunks of whatever it is were bouncing around inside of the cat case and blocking off the exaust flow. Replaced it,runs perfect.Taking cat off my '85 this week. Todd||||reg||1
